              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "What does a neurosurgeon treat in Tashkent?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "A neurosurgeon treats brain, spine and peripheral nerve disease. At NeurON (Tashkent) patients seek care for brain tumors, aneurysms, disc herniation, trigeminal neuralgia and drug-resistant epilepsy."
              }
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "What is neuro-oncology at NeurON?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Neuro-oncology covers diagnosis and surgery for meningioma, glioma, pituitary adenoma and other CNS tumors with MRI planning and MSCT control."
              }
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "How is chronic pain treated at the Pain Center?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Pain Management includes epidural and therapeutic blocks, RFA on COSMAN G4, and PRF for neuropathic pain — often without general anesthesia."
              }
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "Do you offer epilepsy surgery?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Yes. For drug-resistant epilepsy we evaluate removal or modulation of the epileptogenic focus after multidisciplinary work-up."
              }
            }
